    "result_text": "You can now sort a project's invoices by due date, earliest first. `bin/e2e` builds the app and the acceptance test passes.\n\n**What changed:** only `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/invoices/project-invoices.ts`.\n- **Sort button:** the \"Due\" column heading is now a button (`data-testid=\"invoice-sort-due\"`). Clicking it turns the sort on; clicking again goes back to the usual order by invoice number.\n- **Order:** invoices with the same due date are ordered by invoice number.\n- **Accessibility:** the button tells screen readers whether the sort is on, and the column is marked as sorted ascending while it is.\n- **New invoices:** sorting is worked out from the list on screen, so new or paid invoices land in the right place without reloading.\n- **Existing test IDs:** none were renamed or removed.\n\n**Not changed:**\n- **Database and server:** the brief asked for a migration and an OfficeFloor server change, but the server is Spring (OfficeFloor only appears in the Java package name). The page already loads every invoice for the project, so sorting in the browser was enough. The server still returns invoices by ID.\n- **Descending order:** there's no latest-first option. The button only switches between due date (earliest first) and invoice number.",
